WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.540
Requests still start as an email, an attachment, a spreadsheet.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.580
Here, one front door.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.580
Pick the kind.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.060
The form adapts.

5
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.380
Drop the vendor's draft, a managed IT services agreement.

6
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.820
legalVector fills only the empty fields: title, counterparty, contract type, and what

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.020
Legal should know.

8
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.580
Each field says it came from the document.

9
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.020
Undo if you want.

10
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.660
One click sends it.

11
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:32.220
It is now a Legal Request in Doxis: descriptors, file, and a number.

12
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.400
Head of Legal.

13
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:42.160
The daily brief: overdue work, who is overloaded, who has room, which notice deadlines

14
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:42.960
are coming.

15
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.520
Exact figures.

16
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.800
Every line opens its list.

17
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.800
First in, first out.

18
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.720
legalVector suggests a lawyer, with live workload and out of office.

19
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.480
One click assigns.

20
00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:01.680
The process button opens the real workflow diagram: current step, path taken, who did

21
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.880
what, when.

22
00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.880
The assigned lawyer opens the request.

23
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.920
The contract is right there, versions included.

24
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.240
A counterparty mark-up of a mutual non-disclosure agreement.

25
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:21.000
The AI review checks Legal's playbook, clause by clause: thirteen clauses for an NDA.

26
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.720
Watch it work.

27
00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.120
Findings land one at a time, with the rule and proposed wording.

28
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.200
Eight of thirteen pass, with exactly five deviations.

29
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.400
Failing clauses block approval, unless a lawyer overrides them with a reason.

30
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.800
Proposed wording sits with the rule.

31
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.800
Document beside the findings.

32
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.040
Red is missing, amber differs, green complies.

33
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.080
Locate highlights the exact words.

34
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:59.200
Apply change writes a real Word tracked change, lawyer as author, marked AI-assisted.

35
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.040
Insert clause adds the missing text where you click.

36
00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.880
Accept a deviation with a reason and it stays accepted.

37
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:13.200
Save as new version writes that Word file as a new version of the same Doxis document,

38
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.840
and the review runs again.

39
00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.720
In our tests, sixty-two percent became ninety-two.

40
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.000
The Word file and the findings stay side by side.

41
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.980
Approve, with a comment.

42
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.620
The engine task finishes first.

43
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.140
Then the decision hits the descriptors, the timeline, and a Doxis comment on the document.

44
00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.460
The requester gets an email, with a link back.

45
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.620
Not an inbox.

46
00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.980
Not a spreadsheet.

47
00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:44.700
The decision and its reason stay on the document, in Doxis.

48
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.240
Ask from Command K, in plain words.

49
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.880
You get the count, how the question was read, and the matching requests.

50
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.960
Five languages, equally.

51
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.600
Spanish: which confidentiality agreements expire this quarter.

52
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.960
Portuguese: overdue requests.

53
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.840
Then French, and Arabic, right to left.

54
00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.560
Screen, date and number follow the language, light or dark.

55
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.940
legalVector takes requests out of email, spreadsheets and attachments, into Doxis, from

56
00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:30.940
minute one.

57
00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:38.260
It reuses what Doxis already does well: classes, descriptors, versions, comments, permissions

58
00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.420
and workflow.

59
00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.150
Doxis Legal stays the system of record.

